00:36:00.880 --> 00:36:07.620
And something's holding this show together across 310 episodes, and that is the Essential Games List.

00:36:10.800 --> 00:36:19.160
Adventures in the Magic Kingdom is not as good at capturing my imagination of what it's like to go down to Orlando, Florida,

00:36:19.440 --> 00:36:23.540
as the VHS sing-along tape from when I was three years old.

00:36:23.540 --> 00:36:26.700
And I understand that I have nostalgia for that.

00:36:26.700 --> 00:36:33.300
But I would watch that again, both for nostalgic reasons, but also to prove my point here on the show,

00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:40.180
that that has more replayability and had more hours of my time than Adventures in the Magic Kingdom will.

00:36:40.380 --> 00:36:43.160
And it's not that I think Adventures in the Magic Kingdom is a bad game.

00:36:43.160 --> 00:36:50.660
It's a Capcom game, so I think the actual gameplay elements, no matter how short-lived they may be,

00:36:50.820 --> 00:36:53.240
are fine and completely playable.

00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:57.400
I don't have any gripes about the Haunted Mansion stage, right?

00:36:57.460 --> 00:37:01.520
We're not talking about bad enemies or weird controls, right?

00:37:01.540 --> 00:37:04.700
I feel like all the control decisions that they made in the game are fine,

00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:12.440
so the actual game turns out to be this very short, unproductive, not really thought-out experience.

00:37:13.240 --> 00:37:18.980
And so I am not down with the Adventures in the Magic Kingdom.

00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:24.220
I feel like it's just more like time in the Magic Kingdom, and the Adventures will come later.

00:37:24.780 --> 00:37:30.600
Sean? Once again, I have no idea how this compares to actually going to Disney World.

00:37:30.760 --> 00:37:31.640
I wouldn't know.

00:37:31.820 --> 00:37:36.100
But I do like the conceit of this game.

00:37:36.100 --> 00:37:44.140
I do like the idea of the park being like the framing device for all these kind of disparate levels,

00:37:44.180 --> 00:37:49.860
and the fact that they are based off of actual rides is cool,

00:37:49.920 --> 00:37:55.040
and in some ways they're actually, like the gameplay style is based off of what the ride actually is.

00:37:55.140 --> 00:37:56.140
I think that stuff's cool.

00:37:57.980 --> 00:38:02.620
And each of the minigames isn't entirely unplayable.

00:38:02.800 --> 00:38:07.000
